From 80638566686a185dc2abdd15863bd31466412b9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:07:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Model picker and session.create apply the managed
 pin policy

On an example gateway (model_routing.enforce_subscription_only) the Desktop composer offered
gemini-4-argon; session.create stored the pin and the first turn died at agent build, leaving a
chat that can never answer.

- hermes_cli/model_options_managed.py (new): managed_pin_refusal() asks the pin_policy the agent
  build uses whether it would run a (model, provider) pin; drop_refused_managed_pins() narrows
  model.options rows (models, featured_models, unavailable_models, subscription_overlap_models;
  total_models recounted). Hosts without the policy, or with an unreadable one, are unchanged;
  class selectors pass; "" and "custom" rows are refused only when no route registers the model.
- model.options filters after the memo and reads the policy on every call (the memo deep-copies
  on store and hit), and model.save_key's refreshed row (#129260) is narrowed the same way, so
  the picker offers only pins the policy runs.
- session.create refuses a policy-refused pin with -32602 before any session exists, ahead of
  the #96817 catalog-coherence check, judging the pin the way create_overrides stores it. The
  message fits the Desktop toast (summarizeErrorMessage falls back above 180 chars); error data
  carries model, provider and the allowed pins.

Problem: an observed incident on an example gateway, gui.log:<line> `session.create
  20000101_000000_00000a: model=gemini-4-argon provider=gemini source=client override`;
  gui.log:<line> `agent build failed ... ManagedPinRejectedError: Managed subscription policy
  rejects unregistered or ambiguous concrete pin 'gemini-4-argon' on provider 'gemini'`; the
  first prompt.submit failed (gui.log:<line>, errors.log:<line>). state.db keeps that session at
  2 messages, pinned to the refused model.
Why 1: The agent build refused the pin: the hub policy runs subscription routes only, gemini is
  not a subscription provider (agent/model_routing.py:13, :38) and no route registers it.
Why 2: The chat existed with that pin because session.create checked catalog coherence only
  (methods_session_model_guard.model_override_conflict -> static_model_provider_conflict,
  #96817); it never asked pin_policy.
Why 3: The pin was offered because model.options lists every authenticated provider's catalog
  with no policy filter: on the example gateway the offered catalog exceeded the policy allowlist (gemini refused,
  nous refused, openrouter refused; subscription providers partly allowed).
Why 4: The policy was enforced where a pin is used (agent build, and /model since 2e57d4ceef2b)
  but not where a pin is offered or stored; there was no shared "would the policy run this pin?"
  check for model.options and session.create to call.
Root (happened): pin admission lived only at the consumers, so the surfaces that offer
  (model.options, model.save_key) and store (session.create) a pin disagreed with the agent build.
Root (not caught): the model.options and session.create suites (test_model_options_memo.py,
  test_session_create_model_provider_guard.py) run with the policy off; no test composed an
  enforced policy with the picker or session.create.
Recurrence: third occurrence of this class: t_eeeeee0000000009, then t_eeeeee000000000d, fixed
  by 2e57d4ceef2b (/model refuses a rejected pin). That fix guarded switch_model only; a new
  chat's composer pin reaches session.create as a client override and never calls switch_model,
  so the gap stayed open. This change puts the check in one helper that all three surfaces share.
Countermeasures:
- symptom: session.create refuses before any session state - proof:
  tests/tui_gateway/test_session_create_managed_pin_guard.py (10 tests; with the guard as on
  main 4 fail; the message-length assertion failed at 361 chars before the message change).
- root: one shared helper for model.options, model.save_key and session.create - proof:
  tests/hermes_cli/test_model_options_managed_pins.py (7 tests; each mutation fails: no
  model.options filter 2, no save_key narrowing 1, overlap list left unfiltered 3, no
  non-dict row guard 1, memo hit returning the unfiltered cache 1).
- detection: both suites drive the picker, save_key and session.create under an enforced-policy
  fixture, so a regression on any of the three paths fails there. Affected suite (80 files):
  1646 passed; scripts/check --base origin/main: ok.
- deferred: none.
